From 60061bd618f5375ec164016a9cce111a856c235c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Paes <78096758+paesdan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:24:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] build: no Python -- C build helpers, a Go word check

The build ran Python three times: scripts/room-key.py (always),
scripts/glsl2c.py (GPU builds) and scripts/check-words.py (meson test). It
now needs nothing beyond the C compiler, so it also builds with muon, the
C implementation of meson, on systems that carry no Python at all.

- tools/glsl2c.c and tools/room-key.c, built native: true by the build
  itself, write the same headers the scripts wrote (FNV-1a over room.glsl,
  then gpu.c; the shader as a C string, with \ " and ? escaped).
- tools/checkwords: the word-table check as a Go test, with a mutation test
  for each fault it reports. Run it with `cd tools && go test ./...`.
- themes/make-icons.py and themes/contact-sheet.py are gone; the icon SVGs
  they drew stay committed under themes/icons/DEsk.
- The installers no longer install Python for the build (meson brings its
  own where it is used). SHA256SUMS is made again for the changed tree.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Paes <78096758+paesdan@users.noreply.github.com>
